WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.575
The Risk Management Framework, or RMF,

00:00:02.575 --> 00:00:06.510
is a structured approach for managing cybersecurity and privacy risk throughout the

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.330
lifecycle of information systems.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:12.970
It helps organizations make informed decisions about how systems are designed, operated,

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:15.200
protected, assessed, authorized, and monitored.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.080
RMF is closely associated with guidance from the National Institute of Standards and

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:19.880
Technology,

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:20.920
or NIST.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.480
The framework gives organizations a common process for integrating security, privacy,

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.580
and risk management into system development, operations, and governance.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:32.380
A useful way to understand RMF is to see it as lifecycle risk management.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.240
Security is not treated as a single review at the end of a project.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.510
Risk management begins before a system is built, continues while controls are implemented,

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.360
and remains active while the system operates and changes.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.865
RMF helps teams answer practical questions.

00:00:44.865 --> 00:00:45.880
What is the system?

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.420
What information does it process?

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:51.065
What could happen if confidentiality, integrity, or availability were affected?

00:00:51.065 --> 00:00:52.560
Which controls are appropriate?

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.560
Are those controls working?

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:55.749
Who is responsible for accepting remaining risk?

00:00:55.749 --> 00:01:00.020
The framework also creates a common language between technical teams and leadership.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.500
Engineers may focus on implementation details,

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.780
security teams may focus on controls and assessment,

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.955
and executives may focus on risk decisions.

00:01:06.955 --> 00:01:08.560
RMF connects those perspectives.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.120
RMF does not make risk disappear, and it is not only paperwork.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.480
Its value comes from disciplined decisions, documented evidence, clear responsibilities,

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:20.280
and ongoing monitoring that helps the organization understand its risk posture.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.595
This course provides an educational overview of RMF concepts.

00:01:23.595 --> 00:01:28.020
It is not professional legal, regulatory, authorization, accreditation, compliance,

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.315
or risk management guidance.

00:01:29.315 --> 00:01:32.965
The goal is to help you understand the framework and how people across an organization

00:01:32.965 --> 00:01:33.520
support it.
